{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Why do you cry to Me.</b> This teaches that Moses was standing and praying. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: Now is not the time to prolong in prayer, for Israel are in distress (Mekhilta). Another interpretation — 'Why do you cry to Me': the matter depends on Me and not on you, as is said further on, ״עַל בָּנַי וְעַל פֹּעַל יָדַי תְּצַוֻּנִי״ (Isaiah 45)." "<b>Speak to the children of Israel and let them journey.</b> They have only to journey — the sea will not stand before them. So great is the merit of their fathers and the faith that they believed in Me when they went forth, that the sea will split for them (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:12.004047612Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}